       FD  INVOICE-CH-MASTER.
       01  INVOICE-CH-RECORD.
            03  INVOICE-CH-KEY.
                05  INVOICE-CH-INV-NUM       PIC 9(6).
            03 INVOICE-CH-RETURN-CHAR        PIC X.
      *********************************************************************************
      *                                                                               *
      * THIS DATABASE HAS ONE GOAL. TO MAKE THE INVOICE PRGRAM MORE STABLE SO WE KNOW *
      *  WHEN IT HAS FALLEN OVER DURING PROCESSING AND THE STAFF HAVEN'T NOTICED IT.  *
      *  1.  EVERY INVOICE THAT GETS GENERATED WILL OPEN A FILE ON THIS               *
      *      DATA SET WITH THE FIELD INVOICE-CH-KEY BEING THE INVOICE NUMBER          *
      *      BEING PROCESSED.   AT EVERY STAGE OF THE INVOICE WHEN THAT STAGE HAS BEEN*
      *      SUCCESFULLY COMPLETED THE INVOICE PROGRAM COMES BACK TO THIS DATA SET AND*
      *      UPDATES IT WITH A CHAR FROM THE UPDATE ROUTINE WHICH TELLS US HOW FAR    *
      *      THE INVOICE HAS PROCEEDED. SHOULD THE INVOICE PROGRAM COME TO A HALT     *
      *      IN A NEGATIVE WAY BEFORE IT HAS RUN THE FULL UPDATE LIST, THIS RECORD    *
      *      WILL BE INCOMPLETE WHEN WE RUN THE REPORT PROGRAM - STILL TO BE WRITTEN. *
      *      IN THE INVOICE PROGRAM :                                                 *
      *                                                                               *
      *      PR-036 IS THE SECOND ITEM TO BE COMPLETE - PRINTING OF THE INVOICE       *
      *      SO THE INVOICE-RETURN-CHAR ENTRIES WILL BE :                             *
      *                                                                               *
      *      S = UPDATE SEQUENCE STARTED, INVOICE # TAKEN FROM THE PARAMETER FILE     *
      *                                                                               *
      *      A = INVOICE PRINTED                                                      *
      *      B = DR-TRANS RECORD WRITTEN                                              *
      *      C = DEBTOR FILE UPDATED                                                  *
      *      D = SALES-ANALYIS UPDATED                                                *
      *      E = DISTRIBUTION FILE UPDATED                                            *
      *      F = STOCK-FILES UPDATED                                                  *
      *      G = SLREG RECORD FOR THE P/SLIP UPDATED                                  *
      *      H = SLREG RECORD FOR THE INVOICE WRITTEN                                 *
      *      I = STTRANS WRITTEN FOR THE INVOICE                                      *
      *      J = STTRANS RE-WRITTEN FOR THE P/SLIP TO BE UPDATED                      *
      *      K = SOLDBY RECORD WRITTEN FOR INVOICE TOTALS                             *
      *                                                                               *
      *      L = INVOICE RECORD COMPLETED SUCCESFULLY                                 *
      *********************************************************************************
